  "confidence": "Low",
  "rationale": "All three candidates are concept-aligned to vitiligo by trait_reported/trait_efo, but their endpoint fidelity differs materially. PGS000738 has the cleanest-looking vitiligo intent (trait_reported=Vitiligo; disease-focused publication title) and avoids an explicit non-vitiligo, treatment-induced endpoint; by contrast, PGS000760’s phenotyping_reported is explicitly therapy-specific/non-vitiligo (anti-PD-L1 induced hypothyroidism in cancer patients), making it a weaker direct-match vitiligo endpoint despite being labeled Vitiligo. PGS001536 is a UK Biobank pan-trait framework score (\"across 813 traits\"; snpnet) and is additionally time-to-event, both warning signals per the provided domain guidance even though it reports PGS-only AUROC/R2. PGS000738 is selected as best-supported primarily on endpoint/study-context coherence, but confidence is low because PGS000738’s phenotyping_reported is inconsistent with vitiligo (\"Red hair\") and its reported performance evidence is limited/non-PRS-comparable (pseudo R² with unclear covariate context), leaving unresolved metadata/endpoint ambiguity."
}

