  "rationale": "Both available candidates are direct matches to the target trait via trait_efo=\"nicotine dependence\" and consistent phenotyping_reported=\"Tobacco use disorder\", and they come from the same UK Biobank portability publication with similar covariates and training/validation context. The only clear differentiator in the visible evidence is selected European validation performance (partial correlation): PGS002037 has higher partial-r (0.0741; CI 0.0601–0.0881) than PGS001830 (0.0557; CI 0.0416–0.0697), supporting PGS002037 as the better-supported choice. However, overall strength is limited by the framework/portability study context and the absence of standard PRS-comparable AUC/R2 metrics (only partial-r is shown), so the recommendation remains sub-optimal rather than high-confidence."
}
